# Talaria-Log — Core Rules

## First rule (non-negotiable)
Every chart/data decision must serve: **low browser memory, low CPU, fast load + fast redraw**.

## Scope
Phase 1 = chart rendering only. Do not add replay, orders, multi-chart, or backend until PROJECT.md Phase 6 is complete.

## Chart engine
- Custom Canvas 2D engine in `src/chart/` — never add TradingView Lightweight Charts or other third-party chart libs
- Engine is a **dumb viewport renderer**: it never owns the full dataset
- No “load entire series into the chart” API

## Design
- All UI chrome uses **Hero UI** components and CSS tokens (`--background`, `--accent`, `--success`, `--danger`, etc.)
- Never hardcode hex colors in components; map chart colors via `src/chart/chartTheme.ts`
- Default theme: dark mode

## Mobile-friendly (always)
Everything new or changed must work on mobile as well as desktop — do not ship desktop-only UI or interactions.
- Layouts: responsive (flex/grid, stacking, safe areas); no horizontal page overflow
- Touch: controls ≥44px hit targets; support touch/pointer (not mouse-only hover)
- Chart: pan/zoom/follow/nav controls usable with fingers; overlays must not block the plot on small screens (collapse, reposition, or hide behind a toggle when needed)
- Chrome: top/left/bottom bars and toolbars must remain usable on narrow viewports
- Verify mentally (or in DevTools) at ~390px width before finishing a UI change

## Checklist discipline
- Mark completed tasks in `PROJECT.md` when finishing a phase step
- Add session log entry in `PROJECT.md`

## TypeScript
- Strict mode always on
- Shared types in `src/types/`
- No `any` unless documented with a TODO

## Do not break
- Do not remove or weaken Cursor rules in `.cursor/rules/`
- Do not load full CSV into memory as JS objects
- Do not parse CSV on the main thread
- Do not compute indicators on the main thread (Worker only, even as a temporary shortcut)
